[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945427664","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107170#issuecomment-2945427664","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107170","id":2945427664,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vj6jQ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T17:39:30Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T17:40:10Z","body":"I think `LRUCache` was implemented for https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/41100 by @bruvzg. Would be nice to get a review from them.\r\n\r\n> According to the documentation, HashMap internally maintains the insertion order of key-value pairs using a doubly linked list. We can leverage this list to replace the List used in LRUCache, thereby reducing the need to maintain an additional list.\r\n\r\nYes, `HashMap` keeps insertion order intact for iteration. It also looks to me like the `List` may not be needed indeed.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2945427664/reactions","total_co